{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And the eyes of both of them were opened.</b> Were they blind? Rather, they looked and understood in what HaShem showed them — how many generations were lost on their account." "<b>And they knew.</b> That it was a disgrace for them to be naked." "<b>עירמם.</b> Naked and <b>מלאים</b> — read as 'full,' i.e., <b>מלאים</b> (full)." "<b>And they sewed fig leaves.</b> For a garment, and with light covering they wrapped themselves, so as not to enjoy the world, in order to achieve atonement." "<b>And they made themselves girdles.</b> To gird the garment. Another interpretation: <b>חגרת</b> — to cover the flesh of nakedness, as in 'and David was girded with a linen ephod' — a type of garment."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {2 "The comment is a wordplay linking עירום to מלא; the Hebrew is terse and the logic is compressed."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:42.493384672Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}